    "work": "Tao Te Ching",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q003",
    "text": "Little by little, one travels far.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q004",
    "text": "One day at a time.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q005",
    "text": "One step at a time.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q006",
    "text": "Fall seven times, stand up eight.",
    "author": "Japanese proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q007",
    "text": "Hope is the thing with feathers.",
    "author": "Emily Dickinson",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q008",
    "text": "I dwell in Possibility.",
    "author": "Emily Dickinson",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q009",
    "text": "Every day is a new beginning.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q010",
    "text": "Mighty oaks from little acorns grow.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q011",
    "text": "Little strokes fell great oaks.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q012",
    "text": "The first step is always the hardest.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q013",
    "text": "Well begun is half done.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q014",
    "text": "Slowly but surely.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q015",
    "text": "The sun is new each day.",
    "author": "Heraclitus",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q016",
    "text": "But still, like dust, I'll rise.",
    "author": "Maya Angelou",
    "work": "Still I Rise",
    "year": "1978",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q017",
    "text": "Hope is a good thing, maybe the best of things.",
    "author": "Stephen King",
    "work": "Rita Hayworth and Shawshank Redemption",
    "year": "1982",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q018",
    "text": "Go placidly amid the noise and haste.",
    "author": "Max Ehrmann",
    "work": "Desiderata",
    "year": "1927",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q019",
    "text": "Pay attention. Be astonished. Tell about it.",
    "author": "Mary Oliver",
    "work": "Sometimes",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q020",
    "text": "You don't have to see the whole staircase, just take the first step.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q021",
    "text": "Every day is a second chance.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q022",
    "text": "Drop by drop, the bucket fills.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q023",
    "text": "Not all those who wander are lost.",
    "author": "J.R.R. Tolkien",
    "work": "The Fellowship of the Ring",
    "year": "1954",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q024",
    "text": "Step by step, the ladder is climbed.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q025",
    "text": "There is always light, if only we're brave enough to see it.",
    "author": "Amanda Gorman",
    "work": "The Hill We Climb",
    "year": "2021",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q026",
    "text": "Bloom where you are planted.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q027",
    "text": "Today is a new day.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q028",
    "text": "Keep some room in your heart for the unimaginable.",
    "author": "Mary Oliver",
    "work": "Evidence",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q029",
    "text": "Hope is a waking dream.",
    "author": "Aristotle",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q030",
    "text": "Start where you are.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q031",
    "text": "Rome wasn't built in a day.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "any"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q032",
    "text": "Slow and steady wins the race.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "any"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q033",
    "text": "Adopt the pace of nature: her secret is patience.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "any"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q034",
    "text": "Nature does not hurry, yet everything is accomplished.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "any"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q035",
    "text": "Make haste slowly.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "any"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q036",
    "text": "Good things take time.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "any"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q037",
    "text": "Easy does it.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "any"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q038",
    "text": "You can't pour from an empty cup.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "any"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q039",
    "text": "Be gentle with yourself.",
    "author": "Max Ehrmann",
    "work": "Desiderata",
    "year": "1927",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "any"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q040",
    "text": "Go easy on yourself.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "any"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q041",
    "text": "And now that you don't have to be perfect, you can be good.",
    "author": "John Steinbeck",
    "work": "East of Eden",
    "year": "1952",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "any"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q042",
    "text": "Forever is composed of nows.",
    "author": "Emily Dickinson",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "any"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q043",
    "text": "Every flower blooms in its own time.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "any"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q044",
    "text": "Patience and time do more than strength or rage.",
    "author": "Jean de La Fontaine",
    "work": "The Lion and the Rat",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "any"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q045",
    "text": "One kind word can warm three winter months.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "any"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q046",
    "text": "After all, tomorrow is another day.",
    "author": "Margaret Mitchell",
    "work": "Gone with the Wind",
    "year": "1936",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "night"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q047",
    "text": "Tomorrow is a new day with no mistakes in it yet.",
    "author": "L. M. Montgomery",
    "work": "Anne of Green Gables",
    "year": "1908",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "night"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q048",
    "text": "Rest is not idleness.",
    "author": "John Lubbock",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "night"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q049",
    "text": "Night brings counsel.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "night"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q050",
    "text": "Things look better in the morning.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "night"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q051",
    "text": "Sleep on it.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "night"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q052",
    "text": "Only when it is dark enough can you see the stars.",
    "author": "Martin Luther King Jr.",
    "work": "I've Been to the Mountaintop",
    "year": "1968",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "night"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q053",
    "text": "I have loved the stars too fondly to be fearful of the night.",
    "author": "Sarah Williams",
    "work": "The Old Astronomer",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "night"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q054",
    "text": "Finish each day and be done with it.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "night"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q055",
    "text": "The darkest hour is just before the dawn.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "night"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q056",
    "text": "This too shall pass.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "after_hard_day"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q057",
    "text": "No winter lasts forever; no spring skips its turn.",
    "author": "Hal Borland",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "after_hard_day"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q058",
    "text": "If winter comes, can spring be far behind?",
    "author": "Percy Bysshe Shelley",
    "work": "Ode to the West Wind",
    "year": "1820",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "after_hard_day"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q059",
    "text": "In the midst of winter, I found there was, within me, an invincible summer.",
    "author": "Albert Camus",
    "work": "Return to Tipasa",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "after_hard_day"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q060",
    "text": "After rain comes sunshine.",
    "author": "Proverb",
    "work": "",
    "year": "",
    "translator": "",
    "source_url": "",
    "tags": [
      "after_hard_day"
    ]
  }
]
